# Domain vs persistence

Follow `backend/AGENTS.md`. Persistence is **PostgreSQL + Prisma**. Do not add Mongoose or Drizzle.

When adding an aggregate:

1. Domain type in `backend/src/domain/` — `id: string`, no Prisma, no password.
2. Model in `backend/prisma/schema.prisma` — then `prisma migrate`.
3. Repository in `backend/src/repositories/` — maps uuid → `id`; only layer that imports `prisma`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — route/service uses PrismaClient
const row = await prisma.user.findUnique({ where: { email } });
res.json(row);

// ✅ GOOD
const user = await findUserByEmail(email);
if (!user) throw new NotFoundException("User not found");
res.json(user);
```

No generic `Repository<T>`. No Prisma middleware to hash passwords. Hash in `user.service.ts`, persist `passwordHash` via the repo. Login: `findUserCredentialsByEmail` + `comparePassword`.
